            "title": "JPMorgan Stock Drops After Bank Predicts $105 Billion in Expenses Next Year",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "JPMorgan Chase\u2019s stock fell more than 4.7% on Tuesday after the bank told investors that it will spend billions of dollars more in expenses next year.  At the Goldman Sachs conference in New York on Tuesday, consumer chief Marianne Lake told investors that the bank had just completed budgeting for next year and is planning to spend $105 billion, largely because of higher costs in her division.  The bank is expecting expenses this year to be $95.9 billion and analysts had anticipated approximately $101 billion of expenses next year, according to FactSet.",
